{"name":"Barn Red","hex":"#8b4044","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"barn red","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A reddish-brown color like that with which barns are traditionally painted."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barn_red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Barn","blocks":[{"text":"A barn is an agricultural building usually on farms and used for various purposes. In North America, a barn refers to structures that house livestock, including cattle and horses, as well as equipment and fodder, and often grain. As a result, the term barn is often qualified e.g. tobacco barn, dairy barn, cow house, sheep barn, potato barn. In the British Isles and in Europe, the term barn is restricted mainly to storage structures for unthreshed cereals and fodder, the terms byre, shippon or shippen being applied to cow shelters, whereas horses are kept in buildings known as stables. In mainland Europe, however, barns were often part of integrated structures known as byre-dwellings. In addition, barns may be used for equipment storage, as a covered workplace, and for activities such as threshing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Zalmon_Read_Barn_back_view.jpg/330px-Zalmon_Read_Barn_back_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barn","wikidata":"Q1303167"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/TTCdairybarn.jpg/330px-TTCdairybarn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/TTCdairybarn.jpg/330px-TTCdairybarn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Texas Technological College Dairy Barn in Lubbock, Texas, U.S., was used as a teaching facility until 1967.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATTCdairybarn.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/%D0%9B%D0%B5%D0%B1%D0%B5%D0%B4%D0%B5%D0%B2_%D0%93%D1%83%D0%BC%D0%BD%D0%BE_1894.jpg/500px-%D0%9B%D0%B5%D0%B1%D0%B5%D0%B4%D0%B5%D0%B2_%D0%93%D1%83%D0%BC%D0%BD%D0%BE_1894.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/%D0%9B%D0%B5%D0%B1%D0%B5%D0%B4%D0%B5%D0%B2_%D0%93%D1%83%D0%BC%D0%BD%D0%BE_1894.jpg/500px-%D0%9B%D0%B5%D0%B1%D0%B5%D0%B4%D0%B5%D0%B2_%D0%93%D1%83%D0%BC%D0%BD%D0%BE_1894.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Russian women using a hand powered winnowing machine in a threshing barn. Note the board across the doorway to prevent grain from spilling out of the barn, this is the origin of the term threshold.[1] Painting from 1894 by Klavdy Lebedev titled the floor or the threshing floor (Гумно).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A%D0%9B%D0%B5%D0%B1%D0%B5%D0%B4%D0%B5%D0%B2_%D0%93%D1%83%D0%BC%D0%BD%D0%BE_1894.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/GrangeBarn-interior.jpg/500px-GrangeBarn-interior.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conten